SUMMARY:IMPROMPTU LVRT - Colebrook Tavern Ride (30R/14R)
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nRide Leader: Bruce Black\
 n\n**PLEASE NOTE THE START TIME**\n\nAn enjoyable ride starting and ending
  at Lebanon Valley Rail Trail - Cornwall Trailhead and exploring the Cornw
 all and Mt. Gretna area. There will be an alternative start for those who 
 want less mileage at the Lebanon Valley Rail Trail parking area on Colebro
 ok Rd. This alternative start is at the 7-mile mark of the course on the R
 ideWith GPS map in the link below. We will leave the 30-mile start at 9:30
  and leave the alternate start at 10. We will stop at Colebrook Tavern for
  lunch and then meander back to the parking lot via the Lebanon Valley Rai
 l Trail. The pace will be 13 - 15 mph average with multiple regroup points
  (like 4 or 5).\n\nThis ride is a social ride\, but cyclists are not expec
 ted to stay in one group. Cyclists may pedal at their own comfortable pace
 s. Please be supportive of the other cyclists to avoid anyone biking alone
  or being dropped off the back of the last group.\n\nCue and Ride with GPS
  links:\n[https://ridewithgps.com/routes/54714924](https://ridewithgps.com
 /routes/54714924)\n\nHelmets are mandatory\; please also plan to bring 1-2
  water bottles\, and a basic repair kit (spare tube\, tire levers\, pump/C
 O2 inflator).\nBeing a Meetup Member does not mean you are a club member. 
 Use this link to join the club.\n[https://www.lancasterbikeclub.net/conten
 t.aspx?page_id=60&club_id=257148](https://www.lancasterbikeclub.net/conten
 t.aspx?page_id=60&club_id=257148)\nYour RSVP is your agreement to abide by
  the club's Code of Conduct [https://lancbikeclub.clubexpress.com/content.
 aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=323984](https://lancbikeclub.club
 express.com/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=323984)\nand 
 Rules of the Road\n[https://lancbikeclub.clubexpress.com/content.aspx?](ht
 tps://lancbikeclub.clubexpress.com/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&
 module_id=325159)
